/* Every div gets the theme's line height. Only this declaration of the former
   reset changes anything: removing `font-size`/`margin`/`padding: unset` left all
   computed styles identical (scripts/measure-css.mjs compare). A bare tag selector
   is the cheapest way to reach every div; a container prefix would add an
   ancestor check per div.
   The UI font goes on every div too: Roam's site.css sets `div { font-family: Inter }`,
   which stops inheritance, so a font set on body would never reach a div. Blueprint's
   default (Inter) is Roam's own, so nothing changes until a theme or setting sets it. */
